Article 11 Social insurance agencies shall record the following information in a timely, complete, and accurate manner:
(1) Social insurance registration status;
(2) Social insurance premium payment status;
(3) Social insurance benefits receipt status;
(4) Personal account status;
(5) Other information related to social insurance administration.

Article 42 The social insurance agency shall verify the following matters:
(1) the registration of social insurance and the enjoyment of benefits, etc.;
(2) the performance of service agreements by social insurance service institutions and the implementation of expense settlement items and standards;
(3) other matters provided for by laws and regulations.

Article 47 The human resources and social security administrative department and the medical security administrative department shall, in accordance with their respective functions, conduct supervision and inspection over the social insurance agency regarding the following matters:
(1) the implementation of social insurance laws, regulations, and rules;
(2) the operational situation of social insurance registration, benefit payment, etc.;
(3) the management of social insurance funds;
(4) the signing and performance of service agreements with social insurance service institutions;
(5) other matters provided for by laws and regulations.
The finance department and the audit authority shall, in accordance with their respective functions, exercise supervision over the relevant work of the social insurance agency according to law.

Article 53 Where a social insurance agency or any of its staff members commits any of the following acts, the human resources and social security administrative department or the medical security administrative department shall, within its respective functions and duties, order it to make corrections; if losses are caused to the social insurance fund, the employer, or an individual, it shall bear compensation liability according to law; the responsible leaders and the directly responsible persons shall be given sanctions according to law:
(1) Failing to perform the statutory duties of social insurance;
(2) Requiring the provision of evidentiary materials in violation of provisions;
(3) Deducting or refusing to pay social insurance benefits on time;
(4) Losing or tampering with social insurance data such as contribution records and records of enjoyment of social insurance benefits, or personal rights records; or
(5) Violating the internal control system for social insurance handling.
